  "prefLabel": "Plc 202.23 Proceeding",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 202.23 “Proceeding” means the totality of the handling of a matter, including the initiation, review, hearing, decision, and, if applicable, reconsideration or rehearing of the matter. A proceeding can be either adjudicative or non-adjudicative.\n\nSource. #13837, eff 12-28-23 (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Plc 200); ss by #14136, eff 12-1-24 (formerly Plc 202.33)",
